    "body": "Adding `sign_extend: true` to the encoding metadata is incorrect for this instruction because the operation uses `$signed(imm << 5)` rather than just `$signed(imm)`.\n\nWhen `sign_extend: true` is set in the encoding, the 7-bit immediate is sign-extended to full width immediately after extraction. Then, when the operation shifts this already-sign-extended value left by 5, the result is incorrect.\n\nFor example, with a 7-bit immediate of `1010101`:\n- Without `sign_extend: true`: The operation computes `$signed(0b101010100000)`, which correctly sign-extends the 12-bit offset\n- With `sign_extend: true`: The 7 bits are first extended to 64 bits as 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFD5, then shifted to produce an incorrect result\n\nThe correct fix would be to either:\n1. Add `left_shift: 5` to the encoding metadata and change the operation to use `$signed(imm)` instead of `$signed(imm << 5)`, OR\n2. Keep the encoding metadata without `sign_extend: true` since the sign extension semantically needs to happen after the shift in the operation\n\nThis same issue applies to prefetch.r and prefetch.w.",
